<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Didgori</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1121</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Didgori was fought on 12 August 1121 west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tbilisi">Tbilisi</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">King David</a> IV the Builder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> defeated a large Seljuk-led Muslim coalition. The victory allowed David to capture Tbilisi in 1122, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of Tbilisi and making the city his capital. It opened Georgia's golden age of expansion in the twelfth century.</p></div>
